## Key Design Decisions

### 1. Configurable OpenAI Model
```env
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini          # Change to gpt-4o, gpt-4-turbo, etc.
OPENAI_MAX_TOKENS=2048            # Optional override
```
The `aiService.js` reads `OPENAI_MODEL` from config and uses it everywhere. Switch models by changing one line in `.env`.

### 2. Supabase as Real Database
Full SQL schema with 9 tables: `leads`, `deals`, `sequences`, `messages`, `templates`, `settings`, `icp_profiles`, `scheduled_posts`, `agent_runs`. Run the migration in your Supabase dashboard SQL editor. RLS policies included for security.

### 3. Twitter Tier Degradation
```env
TWITTER_TIER=free                  # free | basic | pro
```
| Feature | Free | Basic ($100/mo) | Pro ($5K/mo) |
|---------|------|-----------------|--------------|
| Post tweets | ✅ 1500/mo | ✅ 3000/mo | ✅ 300K/mo |
| Read tweets | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |
| DMs | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Analytics | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Search | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |

### 4. Graceful Degradation Pattern (All Services)
Every service checks if its API key is configured:
- **Configured** → makes real API calls with retries + error handling
- **Not configured** → returns realistic sample data matching Flutter screen expectations

This means the app works out of the box with zero keys, and you light up real integrations one at a time.

---

## Supabase Schema (will be in `supabase_schema.sql`)

9 tables:
- `leads` — All leads from all sources with scoring
- `deals` — Closed revenue deals
- `sequences` — Apollo email sequences tracking
- `messages` — Outreach messages (all channels)
- `templates` — Message templates
- `settings` — App configuration
- `icp_profiles` — Saved Ideal Client Profiles
- `scheduled_posts` — Twitter post scheduler
- `agent_runs` — AI agent execution logs

---

## After Build: Keys & Config You'll Need

Here's everything you'll need to fill in `.env` to get started:

### Essential (get these first)
| Key | Where to get it | Required for |
|-----|----------------|--------------|
| `SUPABASE_URL` | [supabase.com](https://supabase.com) → Project → Settings → API | Database |
| `SUPABASE_KEY` | Same page → `anon` public key | Database |
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | [platform.openai.com](https://platform.openai.com) → API Keys | AI features |

### Integrations (add as needed)
| Key | Where to get it |
|-----|----------------|
| `APOLLO_API_KEY` | [app.apollo.io](https://app.apollo.io) → Settings → Integrations → API |
| `UMAMI_TOKEN` + `UMAMI_SITE_ID` + `UMAMI_BASE_URL` | Your Umami instance → Settings |
| `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN` + `SENTRY_ORG` + `SENTRY_PROJECT` | [sentry.io](https://sentry.io) → Settings → Auth Tokens |
| `TWITTER_BEARER_TOKEN` + OAuth keys | [developer.twitter.com](https://developer.twitter.com) → Dashboard |
| `TRUSTMRR_API_KEY` + `TRUSTMRR_BASE_URL` | TrustMRR dashboard → API |
| `GUMROAD_ACCESS_TOKEN` | [gumroad.com](https://gumroad.com) → Settings → Advanced |
| `AGENTSCOPE_API_KEY` + `AGENTSCOPE_API_URL` | AgentScope dashboard |
| `VERDENT_API_KEY` | Verdent.ai dashboard |
| `HEADAI_API_KEY` | HeadAI dashboard |
| `WEBROBOTS_API_KEY` | WebRobots dashboard |

### Optional / RSS-based
| Key | Default |
|-----|---------|
| `BETALIST_RSS_URL` | `https://betalist.com/feed` |
| `STARTUPSRIP_RSS` | `https://startups.rip/feed` |
| `SOLIDGIGS_INBOUND_EMAIL` | Email forwarding address |
| `CONTRA_INBOUND_EMAIL` | Email forwarding address |

